  description: "His flame soared through the town, and took all of its innocent folk
    with it. No one was spared, not even children. His heart had completely turned
    dark, there was no going back. the townsfolk had been deemed unworthy of his
    knowledge, and so they were to burnt for their illiteracy.\n\nSince no one remembered
    him for his achiements in science and magic, He had decided he would be remembered
    for something far worse. His passion for knowledge turned into passion for intellectual
    purity. \n\nMay the Gods pity those who meet his gaze."
